  "grammarExplanation": "Negative commands in French are very straightforward: they use the exact same forms as Affirmative commands but wrap the verb in 'ne ... pas'.\n\n• Parle (Speak) → Ne parle pas (Don't speak)\n• Mangez (Eat, pl) → Ne mangez pas (Don't eat)\n\nCrucial rule: With negative commands, object pronouns DO NOT attach to the end. They go back to their typical spot BETWEEN 'ne' and the verb:\n• Donne-le-moi (Give it to me) → Ne me le donne pas (Don't give it to me).\n• Dis-lui (Tell him) → Ne lui dis pas (Don't tell him).",
